# Bot1 casts Court of Garenbrig on turn 1 (Black Lotus for {G}{G}{G}) and becomes the monarch. On turn 2 Bot2 casts its own
# Court the same way and becomes the monarch instead (CR 725.2: the designation moves to the player who just became it).
# In Bot1's upkeep on turn 3 the trigger still puts both counters on Ornithopter, but "then if you're the monarch" is false,
# so nothing is doubled: Ornithopter has exactly 2. The monarch is Bot2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Court of Garenbrig
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Court of Garenbrig
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Court of Garenbrig.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Court of Garenbrig.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Divide(Ornithopter: 2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Monarch = Bot2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
